38:Two to four sentences of un-headed opening prose summarizing what the authors measured, what they found, and why it matters. The prose sits directly under the `# H1` title with no `## TL;DR` heading; the wiki reads as authoritative reference, not as a list of casual TL;DRs. Source pages created before 2026-05-08 may still carry the legacy heading; remove it on touch.
128:Stub pages carry only sections 2 (body table, all rows marked data gap) and 8 (source legend with empty-corpus message). When a stub crosses two-plus contributing A-tier sources, the section-completion subprocess action drafts sections 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 from the routing audit and contributing source pages.
253:Inline and table citations on product-category pages use numbered aliases `[[sources/<cite-key>|1]]`. A `Sources` block at the end maps each number to the full source page.

